<!-- @after Internal Mechanics :: animation -->
### Watch the request and response unwind

<section class="pb-figure" data-pb-flow="scene" aria-label="A request goes in; a response returns">
<h3>A request goes in; a response returns</h3>
<p class="pb-sub">An illustrative run. Each moving packet is a named request, notification or result.</p>
<div class="pb-paper"><svg class="pb-svg" role="img" aria-label="An application interceptor calls proceed with a request. A response returns through it to the caller. The HTTP chain includes cache and network handling; it does not always contact a server."></svg></div>
<div class="pb-progress" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
<div class="pb-caption"><span class="pb-count"></span><p aria-live="polite"></p></div>
<div class="pb-controls"><button type="button" class="pb-btn" data-act="prev">Previous</button><button type="button" class="pb-btn primary" data-act="play" aria-pressed="false">Play</button><button type="button" class="pb-btn" data-act="next">Next</button><span class="spacer"></span><button type="button" class="pb-btn" data-act="reset">Reset</button></div>
<details class="pb-steps"><summary>Read every step as text</summary><ol></ol></details>
<script type="application/json">{"nodes": [{"id": "call", "label": "Caller"}, {"id": "middleware", "label": "App interceptor"}, {"id": "http", "label": "HTTP chain"}], "layouts": {"wide": {"size": [760, 260], "nodes": {"call": {"x": 24, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}, "middleware": {"x": 276, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}, "http": {"x": 528, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}}, "edges": {"enter": "M234 86 L274 86", "proceed": "M486 86 L526 86", "return": "M526 130 L486 130", "deliver": "M274 130 L234 130"}, "labels": []}, "narrow": {"size": [320, 500], "nodes": {"call": {"x": 40, "y": 26, "w": 240, "h": 88}, "middleware": {"x": 40, "y": 182, "w": 240, "h": 88}, "http": {"x": 40, "y": 338, "w": 240, "h": 88}}, "edges": {"enter": "M120 116 L120 180", "proceed": "M120 272 L120 336", "return": "M200 336 L200 272", "deliver": "M200 180 L200 116"}, "labels": [], "pk": {"dx": 10, "dy": 5, "anchor": "start"}}}, "modes": {"run": {"initial": {"nodes": {"call": ["", "GET /profile"], "middleware": ["", "not entered"], "http": ["", "cache or network"]}}, "steps": [{"caption": "The caller starts an OkHttp call. This scene follows one application interceptor; Retrofit can construct the request above this boundary."}, {"caption": "The application interceptor receives the request. Interceptors run in registration order. This one inspects the request without consuming a response body.", "packets": [{"edge": "enter", "label": "request", "tone": "fwd"}], "set": {"nodes": {"middleware": ["is-active", "inspect request"]}}}, {"caption": "Calling chain.proceed(request) enters the rest of the chain. A cache hit can satisfy it without a network exchange.", "packets": [{"edge": "proceed", "label": "proceed", "tone": "fwd"}], "set": {"nodes": {"middleware": ["", "waiting for response"], "http": ["is-active", "resolve request"]}}}, {"caption": "A response returns to the interceptor. Response direction reverses the call path. Application interceptors observe the final response across redirects; network interceptors can observe individual exchanges.", "packets": [{"edge": "return", "label": "response", "tone": "back"}], "set": {"nodes": {"http": ["is-done", "response ready"], "middleware": ["is-active", "inspect response"]}}}, {"caption": "The interceptor returns the response to its caller. A logger must not consume the one-shot body and leave it empty for the converter or application.", "packets": [{"edge": "deliver", "label": "response", "tone": "back"}], "set": {"nodes": {"middleware": ["is-done", "returned response"], "call": ["is-active", "owns response body"]}}}, {"caption": "The caller consumes and closes the body. An interceptor that calls proceed again must close the previous response body first.", "set": {"nodes": {"call": ["is-done", "body closed"]}}}]}}}</script>
<p class="pb-sub">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/square/okhttp/blob/master/docs/features/interceptors.md">OkHttp interceptor guide</a>.</p>
